In the past, Dr. Rickman fought the younger [[Dante Vale]] on a clifftop in [[Jericho, Palestine]] for an ancient native Mexican bowl. He won the altercation by using his powerful Titan [[Wendigo]] and provoking Dante by taunting him into a fight. He then mocked Dante for his hot-headed nature, a memory which stuck with him for years. {{source|Mission to Skara Brae}} 

Rickman came face to face with Dante many years later in the village of Skara Brae, on a mission to uncover the secret behind the ancient [[Jadeite Necklace]], a mission given to him by [[The Professor]] himself. He pursued the team and fought against [[Zhalia Moon]] and her [[King Basilisk]] before sending [[Gregor]], his new addition to his team, to eliminate the Huntik team .{{source|Mission to Skara Brae}}

Rickman later sent his agents, [[Celina]] and [[Bonnie]] to pursue [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] but they failed. Later, Rickman invoked Silver Hunter in to attack Dante in [[Quimper Cathedral]]. After defeating Dante's [[Solwing]], it fought against [[Caliban]] who was sent back to his Amulet by Rickman's spell. Silver Hunter knocked Dante to the floor but was turned to stone by [[King Basilisk]] before he could finish him off. Rickman later arrived at Ys with back up from his team and [[Captain Caine]]. {{source|The Seekers of Ys}} 

Rickman summoned Silver Hunter in the underwater city of Ys, to hunt down Dante, but it was defeated by Dante's [[Metagolem]]. He then invoke [[Wendigo]], reminding Dante of how he first beat him, but he was knocked unconscious by Dante and arrested by the [[Huntik Foundation]] along with Celina, Bonnie, [[Gregor]], [[Captain Caine]] and [[Ford]]. {{source|The Lost City of Casterwill}}

Dr. Rickman is an extremely astute [[Seeker]] who is able to outsmart opponents by sening their insecurities and weaknesses. He is extremely expeirenced, and can sense magical properties such [[Thoughtspecter]] illusions. His combat abilities were able to overpower those of Dante's showing him to be a formidable and powerful enemy.
